From fc6cbc7637b432fc2a7009cb18c8bf5a3b368fdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romeu Melur <romeumello@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:10:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/fs: allow configuring lookup and attribute cache
 timeouts

Passthrough filesystems let the guest cache entries and attributes for
5 s. When the host changes a shared directory, the guest keeps the old
size of a file that grew and reads truncated contents until the timeout
expires; editors that save by rename leave it reading the replaced file.

Expose FsDevice::set_cache_timeouts() in the Rust and C APIs to set the
entry and attribute timeouts in milliseconds, keeping 5000 ms as the
default. LinuxSimplified still never caches attributes; the requested
attribute timeout is kept and applied when switching to LinuxComplete.
NullFs devices reject the call. Update documentation, regenerate
bindings, and add unit tests and an end-to-end regression for a host
growing, creating and replacing files while the guest uses them.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Romeu Melur <romeumello@icloud.com>
